  {
   "id": "01.4",
   "movement": "AS DARK AS BLACK",
   "seconds": 14,
   "lines": "crashing the party / of your evilest instincts / to find vibrations / that echo in silence— / love & hate languages / that translate in / slow dripping blood / salivating on / imminent doubts— / fully awakening / to our darkest night. / pause for a second / a spectrum of / feels—will threads / needles of garments / made of / sweet memories— / in photographs, / film & fiction that / leave me empty. / with your back / faced against me— / you offer me a new / pursuit of happiness / as I stumble / on my own words, / landing into / the secret of— / where you go when you / leave— / & I fall out of life.",
   "treatment": "POET crashes into old-time vintage party, guests are in romantic slow-motion, lots of euphoric light leakage. Poet follows and chases EX (face never shown) around party, through crowd but EX keeps vanishing. Poet trips through hole in the floor, and continue to fall into pure blackness.",
